Two parts of this repository are not covered by that license.

  1. The interface components in `src/ui/` come from Toolcraft by Pixel Point.
     They are used under the Toolcraft Designer License. That license does not
     permit selling this application as a product, or including it in a paid AI
     software product, app builder, website builder, design-to-code service,
     template marketplace or competing generator. Those uses need a separate
     commercial license from Pixel Point. See NOTICE.md.

  2. The sample font at `src/assets/typeforge-sample.ttf` is a subset of DejaVu
     Sans. It is covered by the Bitstream Vera Fonts Copyright. See
     LICENSE-sample-font.txt.

Everything else in this repository is covered by the MIT License, including all
of `src/font/`, which is original work.

Because of the first exception, this repository as a whole is not MIT. If you
want to ship Typeforge as a product, you have to replace `src/ui/` first, or buy
a commercial license from Pixel Point.

